/*.md
scripts/
!scripts/container-start.sh
!scripts/bot-entrypoint.sh
!scripts/setup-cline-auth.sh
!scripts/swarm-bot-lifecycle.sh
# Argo DAG hooks (ADR-078 §1) — the WorkflowTemplate execs these directly; without these
# allowlist entries the Dockerfile COPY fails at build (context excludes scripts/ by default).
!scripts/bot-node-batch.sh
!scripts/finalize-incident.sh
!scripts/record-cost.sh
# Postflight verification trio (INSTALLER-GAPS G1) — extracted from the image by
# oshal-install.sh registry mode; /api/readiness reads the critical-bots list.
!scripts/oshal-verify.sh
!scripts/swarm-routability-check.sh
!scripts/routability-critical-bots.txt
# All OSHAL connector/app CLIs are runtime-required — keep them ALL in the build
# context so every app (walmart, uber, spotify, duffel, …) survives a container
# recreate. New oshal-*.js CLIs are included automatically.
!scripts/oshal-*.js
# The CLIs' shared helpers (exact-user-subject, connector-token-crypto) were extracted to
# scripts/lib/ on 2026-08-05 and 36 require() sites now point there — but this allowlist never
# learned that, so every image built after the extraction shipped CLIs that die at require()
# ("Cannot find module './lib/exact-user-subject'"), which took down the eats/purchasing/rides/
# travel route mounts on 2026-08-06. Top-level *.js ONLY — the .ts tooling, gha/, and
# google-workspace/ under lib/ are not required by any shipped CLI and stay out of the image.
# Guard: tests/unit/image-ships-cli-lib-deps.spec.ts.
!scripts/lib/*.js
# (the swarm CLI moved to packages/swarm-cli — a real npm package, installed globally in the
#  image; packages/ is not excluded, so it needs no allowlist entry here.)
!scripts/migrations/
# Dockerfile.oshal COPYs scripts/governance/ (app-role provisioning) — keep it in context.
!scripts/governance/
/*.bat
/*.sh
oshal.*
docker
infra
checkin-*.log
updated_master_list*
config-output
example-configs

# ── Operator-local secrets: NEVER in any build context ─────────────────────────
# git-archive builds (oshal-deploy.sh) exclude these by being untracked; these entries are the
# defense-in-depth for a hand-run `docker build .` from a working tree where they DO exist.
# The tracked, non-secret seed files (global-config.json, profiles/) stay in context — the
# Dockerfile bakes them to /app/config-seed.dist/ for the registry installer.
config-seed/secrets.json
config-seed/claude-credentials.json
config-seed/*credentials*
config-seed/*.key
.env
.env.*

# The dist-compose generator runs at image build (scripts/ is excluded by default above).
!scripts/gen-dist-compose.js
